{"sourceSha256": "aebcbea3ac3f3eb3aed78a677ffd3db276fbadc7ff6f5fa0e95f76018f32032d", "text": "Ticket Id: 25298\n\nDr Andrew McDonald\nGeneral surgeon\nNorth Melburne Private Hospital\n86 Elm Road\nNorth Melboune 3051\n\n23/1/ 2007\n\nDear Dr McDonald,\nRE: Mrs Daniela Starkovic\n\nThank you for seeing Mrs Starkovic, a 45-year-old married woman whose features are suggestive of\ncholelithiasis.\n\nMrs Starkovic firstly presented on the 20th of January 2007 with a 10 day history of epigastric pain. Her      Comment [teacher1]: days\npain was radiating to the right side, associated with nausea and constant for an hour. At night before she     Comment [teacher2]: The\nvisited me, the pain exacerbated as it was constant for 2 hours, colicky in nature, associated with vomiting\nand not relieved by Aspirin. On examination, mild tenderness in the right upper quadrant of the abdomen        Comment [teacher3]: a\nwas detected. Otherwise, no abnormalities were observed.\n\nToday, the patient was anxious and thinking of acquiring abdominal cancer in spite of cessation of pain.\nLaboratory results revealed mild elevation of alkaline phosphatase level. Ultrasound showed multiple\ngallstones in a small contracted gall bladder.\n\nIn view of the above, my provisional diagnosis is gall bladder inflammation and I reassured the patient\nregarding the possibility of cancer. I would really appreciate it if you provide an assessment of Mrs\nStarkovic and further management of her condition including the possibility of surgical management.\n\nFor any queries, please do not hesitate to contact me.\n\nYours sincerely\n\nDoctor\n\n                                     Report\n Word length                  189\n Comments                     This is a very well written letter!\n Estimated Grade              B+ or A\n Advice                       1. Always proofread the letter after finishing it.\n                              2. Keep up the good work!\n Helpful links                https://www.b